---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { LEGAL } from '../lib/legal';
const contact = LEGAL.contactEmail;
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy policy" description="What Dark Romance Fan collects when you read, comment, rate books or join the newsletter, and how to have it removed.">
  <p>Dark Romance Fan (darkromancefan.com) is a book recommendation site run by one person. This page explains what we collect, why, and what you can ask us to do with it. We don't sell your data and we don't show third-party ads.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you just browse</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A reader cookie (<code>drf_vid</code>).</strong> A random ID that lets us count one rating, trope vote and reaction per browser. It doesn't contain your name or email and lasts up to two years.</li>
    <li><strong>Visit statistics.</strong> We use Vercel Web Analytics, which counts page views without cookies and without building a profile of you.</li>
    <li><strong>Buy-link clicks.</strong> When you click a store link we record which book and which store, and the time. Nothing that identifies you.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host, Vercel, keeps short-lived technical logs (such as IP address and browser type) to run and protect the site.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>When you comment</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your <strong>name</strong> (shown with your comment) and <strong>email address</strong> (never shown). We use your email to recognise returning commenters so their comments can post straight away, and to deal with abuse.</li>
    <li>Your comment, and a <strong>scrambled (hashed) version of your IP address</strong>, used to slow down spam. We can't turn it back into your IP address.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>When you join the Dark Romance Fan newsletter</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your <strong>email address</strong> and where you signed up (for example, the homepage or a comment form). It's stored on our database and passed to our newsletter provider, Kit (kit.com), which sends the emails. Every email has an unsubscribe link.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>When you suggest a book or report a comment</h3>
  <ul><li>What you type, plus a hashed IP address to stop spam.</li></ul>
  <h3>When an author books a promo</h3>
  <ul><li>Payment is handled by Stripe. We receive the author's name, email, book title, book link, preferred date and the amount paid. We never see card details.</li></ul>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> because you asked for it (your consent). You can withdraw it any time by unsubscribing.</li>
    <li><strong>Comments, ratings, moderation and spam protection:</strong> to run the site's reader features safely (our legitimate interests).</li>
    <li><strong>Promo bookings:</strong> to deliver the promotion the author paid for (a contract).</li>
    <li><strong>Visit statistics and click counts:</strong> to see which books readers like, and keep the site useful (our legitimate interests).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the site and provides visit statistics.</li>
    <li><strong>Neon</strong> hosts our database (in the United States).</li>
    <li><strong>Kit</strong> (kit.com) sends the newsletter.</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> takes promo payments.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves the site's fonts, so your browser connects to Google when a page loads.</li>
    <li><strong>Amazon and Bookshop.org</strong> receive you when you click a buy link. They may set their own cookies on their sites to credit us with a commission. Their privacy policies apply there.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some of these companies are based in the United States, so your data may be processed outside the UK and EU under their standard safeguards.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Comments stay up until you ask us to remove them or we take them down.</li>
    <li>Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them.</li>
    <li>Promo booking records are kept as long as we need them for accounts and tax.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask to see the data we hold about you, correct it, delete it, or object to how we use it. {contact ? <>Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a></> : <>Contact us using the email address below</>} and we'll reply within a month. If you're in the UK you can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk); in the EU, to your local data protection authority.</p>
  {!contact && <p class="meta"><strong>Contact email:</strong> to be added by the site owner before this page goes live.</p>}

  <h2>Age</h2>
  <p>This site is for adults. We don't knowingly collect data from anyone under 18. See our <a href="/18-plus">18+ notice</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy we'll update the date at the top of this page.</p>
</LegalPage>
